@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+---
+"@x402/extensions": patch
+---
+
+`validateDiscoveryExtension` now validates Bazaar extension info with an interpreting JSON Schema validator (`@cfworker/json-schema`) instead of compiling the route author's schema with Ajv on every call. Ajv's `compile` uses `new Function()`, which Cloudflare Workers forbid during request handling, so on workerd every valid extension was reported as `valid: false` ("Code generation from strings disallowed for this context") and each request paid for a failed compile. The validator now runs identically on Node, bundlers and Workers, never generates code at runtime, and has no per-call compilation step.
+
+Compatibility notes: `format` keywords stay annotation-only by default, as before; pass `{ assertFormats: true }` to enforce well-known formats (`uri`, `date-time`, `email`, `uuid`, ...). A non-object `schema` and a `$schema` other than JSON Schema 2020-12 are now rejected with explicit errors instead of failing at compile time. Fractional `multipleOf` divisors are compared with a small tolerance (0.3 is accepted as a multiple of 0.1), where the previous implementation compared the raw floating-point quotient and rejected such pairs. Validation error wording has changed.
